<title>ITALY: ALPINE SKIING-ITALY'S COMPAGNONI WINS GIANT SLALOM.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-ITALY'S COMPAGNONI WINS GIANT SLALOM.</headline>
<dateline>SESTRIERE, Italy 1997-02-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deborah Compagnoni of Italy won the women's giant slalom gold medal at the Alpine skiing world championships on Sunday in a time of two minutes 39.19 seconds, according to provisional results.</p>
<p>Karin Roten of Switzerland took the silver in 2:39.99 and Leila Piccard of France the bronze in 2:40.95.</p>
